# Volley (optional, secondary)

> Real-time coordination layer (MQTT topic convention + JSON envelope). This is OPTIONAL
> and SECONDARY. The file-based drop-box (`.agents/memory/` + `.agents/handoffs/`) is the
> primary, mission-critical coordination mechanism.

## Status
- Not yet configured. Enable only if sub-second, cross-process coordination is required.
- Runtime artifacts are gitignored; do not commit them.

## Topics (convention)
- `volley/<project>/status` — agent status heartbeats
- `volley/<project>/mailbox/<agent>` — agent-to-agent messages
- `volley/<project>/progress` — task progress
- `volley/<project>/result` — task results

## Notes
- Prefer the file-based drop-box for auditability and offline resilience.
- Use Volley only when event-driven coordination across machines/processes is required.
